WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.240
Google’s new text to video AI has amazing&nbsp;
capabilities that I have not expected. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:13.520
has learned on 10 billion video tokens,&nbsp;
little pieces, so what did it learn?

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:19.920
For instance, it can create a minute-long movie&nbsp;
about Rookie the Raccoon, and the script for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:27.960
this movie was also written by an AI. That&nbsp;
is excellent, but I expected that. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:35.560
what I did not expect was this, and&nbsp;
this, and this. And there’s so much more.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.160
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.840
Yes, it can do the usual suspects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:48.360
text to video. You provide a text&nbsp;
snippet, and out comes all this.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.960
However, even in that, it can give us something&nbsp;
new. For instance, it can create longer videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:01.720
than most previous systems. Some of these&nbsp;
results can become longer than 15 seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:08.160
so we don’t have to splice a movie together&nbsp;
from these small, 4-second cuts like with many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:15.120
previous techniques. Now temporal coherence is not&nbsp;
perfect in these cases, so the scene can change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:22.680
unexpectedly over time, but it is so much better&nbsp;
than anything else I’ve seen so far. Great work.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:28.440
But, it can do so much more. For&nbsp;
instance, wait, films need sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:34.520
too, right? Can an AI help us with that?&nbsp;
Now hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:43.120
because this AI has also learned on 58 billion&nbsp;
audio tokens. So what did it learn? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:50.280
let’s listen together and take a careful look at&nbsp;
how good it is in making sure that the sounds line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:02:06.720
up with the motions in the video. These were&nbsp;
real good, wow, what an incredible new tool!

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:13.240
We can also perform controllable video editing.&nbsp;
For instance, if we are asking for a raccoon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:21.200
dancing in Times Square, we get this. Okay, but&nbsp;
we are experienced Fellow Scholars over here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.360
we ask okay, but what kind of&nbsp;
dancing are we talking about? And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:34.760
oh yes. We can ask it to do the robot, and&nbsp;
then, hmm…the dance will indeed resemble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:41.960
the robot dance. Or how about this one?&nbsp;
Nice and fluid hip movements. Very sharp.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:49.680
Now, it can also do interactive video editing.&nbsp;
This is amazing. First, after writing the prompt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:55.840
about this rusty steampunk robot, we don’t&nbsp;
just have to accept this one. No sir! We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:02.520
can generate several candidates, and if any&nbsp;
of those caught our eye, we can even extend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:09.560
it. This is due to the technique’s autoregressive&nbsp;
nature, it sees the world as a series of tokens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:16.280
a series of numbers and characters if you will,&nbsp;
and thus, we can easily ask it to extend the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:23.680
video with or without a prompt, thus creating&nbsp;
a system that is art directable! So good!

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.800
And if we can’t write a prompt for something,&nbsp;
because we have something really specific in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:37.520
just add an image. And then, look, it will make it&nbsp;
come alive! So that Mona Lisa can start yawning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:44.160
or that wanderer with the Klaus Kinski-like&nbsp;
hair can marvel at this beautiful , windy place.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.200
And if we are happy with the idea&nbsp;
of the movie, but we would like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:53.120
to try different stylizations of&nbsp;
it, we can try them immediately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:59.200
creating completely different kinds of&nbsp;
moods for the same, or very similar content.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:06.320
And what you see here are just the trivial&nbsp;
cases of stylization. Now let’s bring in the big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:12.960
guns. If we like these teddy bears, and have the&nbsp;
feeling that the floor looks beautifully glossy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:20.960
almost like ice. And then, bam! There we go.&nbsp;
Ice skating in a winter wonderland. Loving it.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:26.920
Or if you feel like this wombat looks like&nbsp;
someone on the beach with a beach ball in hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:30.640
there you go! I can only imagine what miracles you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.880
smart and creative Fellow Scholars will be&nbsp;
able to do create with this in the future.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:41.200
And you even get to control the camera&nbsp;
motions in these videos as well.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:47.080
And you haven’t even heard about the&nbsp;
two coolest things about this work. One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:53.800
if you feel that this tool can do absolutely&nbsp;
everything, you are completely right. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.040
everything is optional here.&nbsp;
Just chuck in whatever you want,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:04.480
even a small piece of an image that you would&nbsp;
like to make a video of, but at the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:12.640
extend it via outpainting, that is also&nbsp;
possible. Mind-blowing. This is the full package.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:20.040
And it gets better. Two, it can do all of these,&nbsp;
in a zero-shot manner. It can synthesize things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:27.120
it hasn’t seen before. That bends the mind&nbsp;
a little, so a word on that. Essentially it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:33.480
means that we can ask it to create something that&nbsp;
it does not have in its training set. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.920
it can lean on its already existing knowledge&nbsp;
about the world. For instance, if you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.760
asking for a vehicle, that vehicle&nbsp;
should probably have a steering wheel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:48.800
or some mechanism for controlling it.&nbsp;
And so on. It is a bit like an actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:56.000
who can improvise a new scene when given a&nbsp;
description. But wait, we are still not done!

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.440
So, how quick is it? It is not in&nbsp;
the order of seconds per frame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:07.960
but frames per second. So we get&nbsp;
one second of video every 4-5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:14.480
seconds. That is absolutely amazing!&nbsp;
I consider that to be blazing fast.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:21.880
Marvelous as this paper is, of course, it is&nbsp;
still not perfect. There are tradeoffs to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:27.040
taken here. For instance, the resolution&nbsp;
of these videos is not the greatest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:33.560
something that can be remedied by current&nbsp;
super resolution tools, and of course, just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:40.480
imagine what we will be capable of just two more&nbsp;
papers down the line. What a time to be alive!

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:48.960
And just as I finish with all this, what do I&nbsp;
see? Oh my. An even better video generator paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:54.120
from Google. Before you ask, of course,&nbsp;
we are going to talk about this one too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.120 --> 00:07:00.000
